  "content": {
    "id": "p26-q15-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "The general form of a quadratic with zeroes $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ is $y=a(x-\\alpha)(x-\\beta)$. Find $a$ in terms of $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ if:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p26-q15-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "the $y$-intercept is $c$,",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=\\dfrac{c}{\\alpha\\beta}$.",
          "worked": "At the $y$-intercept, $x=0$ and $y=c$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}c&=a(0-\\alpha)(0-\\beta)\\\\c&=a\\alpha\\beta\\\\a&=\\frac{c}{\\alpha\\beta}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q15-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "the coefficient of $x$ is $b$,",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=-\\dfrac{b}{\\alpha+\\beta}$.\n\nExpand the factored form and equate the coefficient of $x$ to $b$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=a(x-\\alpha)(x-\\beta)\\\\y&=a\\bigl(x^2-(\\alpha+\\beta)x+\\alpha\\beta\\bigr)\\\\y&=ax^2-a(\\alpha+\\beta)x+a\\alpha\\beta\\end{align*}$$\nThe coefficient of $x$ is $b$, so\n$$\\begin{align*}b&=-a(\\alpha+\\beta)\\\\a&=-\\frac{b}{\\alpha+\\beta}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q15-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "the curve passes through $(1,2)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=\\dfrac{2}{(1-\\alpha)(1-\\beta)}$.",
          "worked": "Substitute $(x,y)=(1,2)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2&=a(1-\\alpha)(1-\\beta)\\\\a&=\\frac{2}{(1-\\alpha)(1-\\beta)}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 29
      }
    ]
  },
